## Golden Example 3 — browser_mod Popup with Action Choices

Use `fire-dom-event` + `browser_mod.popup` for on-device confirmation dialogs. The popup always appears on the device that triggered the action.

```yaml
- type: custom:mushroom-template-card
  primary: Movie Time
  secondary: Lights + Blinds?
  icon: mdi:movie-play
  icon_color: purple
  layout: vertical
  fill_container: true
  tap_action:
    action: fire-dom-event
    browser_mod:
      service: browser_mod.popup
      data:
        title: Movie Time
        size: normal
        content:
          type: vertical-stack
          cards:
            - type: custom:mushroom-template-card
              primary: Lights will be turned off
              secondary: Living Room, Kitchen & Office. Close blinds too?
              icon: mdi:movie-play-outline
              icon_color: purple
              layout: horizontal
              fill_container: true
            - type: horizontal-stack
              cards:
                - type: custom:mushroom-template-card
                  primary: Lights Only
                  icon: mdi:lightbulb-off-outline
                  icon_color: yellow
                  layout: vertical
                  fill_container: true
                  tap_action:
                    action: call-service
                    service: script.turn_on
                    service_data:
                      entity_id: script.movie_time_lights_only
                - type: custom:mushroom-template-card
                  primary: Lights + Blinds
                  icon: mdi:blinds
                  icon_color: blue
                  layout: vertical
                  fill_container: true
                  tap_action:
                    action: call-service
                    service: script.turn_on
                    service_data:
                      entity_id: script.movie_time_lights_and_blinds
```

---

## Service Call Style

Always use the `call-service` / `service:` form (not `perform-action`) for reliability:

```yaml
tap_action:
  action: call-service
  service: script.turn_on
  service_data:
    entity_id: script.good_night_event
```

Git sync pull/push calls `shell_command.ha_pull_config` / `shell_command.ha_push_config` directly with `action: call-service`.

